# What ships is the web app: index.html, src, assets, and the config that builds
# them. Everything below is either regenerated, enormous, or only ever mattered
# on this machine.
#
# Source is kept even when the site does not serve it. The C# engine is half the
# project and the only thing the TypeScript side checks itself against, and these
# are all needed by .github/workflows/deploy.yml, which gates the Pages deploy on
# `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` before it builds:
#   tests/, conformance/cards.json, replays/   `npm test` runs before the build
#   scripts/, worker/                          `npm run typecheck` covers both
# Dropping those does not slim the site down, it just stops it deploying.

# --- build output and dependencies ------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
*.local
*.log

# --- training and measurement output ----------------------------------------
# runs/ alone is around 600 MB of tournament output.
runs/
rarity-snapshot.json

# --- working notes and backups ----------------------------------------------
claude-notes/
card-backups/
Notes.txt
Example board for a player.png

# --- editor and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- .NET build output ------------------------------------------------------
# The C# source under csharp/ is tracked; only what dotnet regenerates is not.
bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
*.nupkg

# bwp theme snapshots
src/.bwp/
